# TEMPLATE — the real file is /etc/alertmanager/slack_webhook_url (NOT in git).
#
# Alertmanager reads the Slack incoming-webhook URL from this file (slack_configs.api_url_file)
# so the secret never lands in alertmanager.yml or the repo. The file must contain ONLY the URL
# on a single line (no quotes, no key=, no trailing comment) — api_url_file reads the whole file
# as the URL.
#
# Provision it:
#   sudo install -d -m 0755 /etc/alertmanager
#   printf '%s' 'https://hooks.slack.com/services/T.../B.../XXXXXXXX' | sudo tee /etc/alertmanager/slack_webhook_url >/dev/null
#   sudo chown root:prometheus /etc/alertmanager/slack_webhook_url
#   sudo chmod 0640 /etc/alertmanager/slack_webhook_url      # root writes, the prometheus user (Alertmanager) reads
#   sudo systemctl reload prometheus-alertmanager
#
# Where the URL comes from: the dedicated "proximal-alerts" Slack app (workspace gearheads),
# api.slack.com/apps → proximal-alerts → Incoming Webhooks → "Add New Webhook to Workspace"
# → pick #proximal-alerts. The app itself is created from proximal-alerts.slack-manifest.json.

https://hooks.slack.com/services/REPLACE_WITH_REAL_WEBHOOK_URL
